<title>BRAZIL: Warm, dry weather holds in Brazil CS sugar areas.</title>
<headline>Warm, dry weather holds in Brazil CS sugar areas.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Warm, dry weather is continuing throughout the sugar cane growing region in Brazil's center-south, independent consultants DataNet-AgriCommodities said in a regular weather update.</p>
<p>During the past week, there was a slight decline in minimum temperatures in producing areas in Sao Paulo and Parana states.</p>
<p>With the cooler mornings and absence of rain, conditions are improving for the maturation of the sugar cane which should raise the sugar content. Maximum temperatures should however remain on the high side, Datanet said.</p>
<p>The rain-free conditions should also mean no delays in sugar loadings at center-south ports, it added.</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
